/T (    Next weekend, we celebrate the start of a new liturgical year with the First Sunday of Advent. This new year will continue our three-year lectionary cycle as we enter into Year B and the Gospel of St. Mark, with a brief interlude from the Gospel of St. John and the Bread of Life Discourse in the middle of Ordinary Time. This structure places the Eucharist at the very center of our lectionary cycle.)
/E (    Next weekend, we celebrate the start of a new liturgical year with the First Sunday of Advent. This new year will continue our three-year lectionary cycle as we enter into Year B and the Gospel of St. Mark, with a brief interlude from the Gospel of St. John and the Bread of Life Discourse in the middle of Ordinary Time. This structure places the Eucharist at the very center of our lectionary cycle.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [78]
